DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: NWO SSH Open Competition – Expand 2026
DESCRIPTION:NWO. New SSH Open Competition instrument (merging the former M
  and L) for curiosity-driven research with a primary social-science or hu
 manities question\; interdisciplinary proposals are allowed. Requests ran
 ge from €350\,000 to €800\,000 for projects of up to six years\, from
  a total budget of €40M. The main applicant needs a PhD and a permanent
  or tenure-track position at a Dutch research institution. Pre-proposals 
 are due 17 Nov 2026 (14:00 CET) and full proposals 10 Jun 2027 (14:00 CES
 T).\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-expand-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-expand-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-186-20261120@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: SME Call 2027 (MKB Call)
DESCRIPTION:Health~Holland (TKI LSH). Health~Holland call for public-priva
 te R&D projects between SMEs and research organisations (industrial resea
 rch\, TRL 4-6\, max 2 years). Consortia can request EUR 225\,000-450\,000
  in PPP subsidy (research organisations max EUR 150\,000 per project)\, a
 t least EUR 8M total for about 20 projects. The lead applicant must be a 
 Dutch for-profit company\, and all partners must co-finance. Full applica
 tions are due 20 November 2026\, 17:00 CET.\n\nhttps://www.health-holland
 .com/en/calls/mkb-call-2027
URL:https://www.health-holland.com/en/calls/mkb-call-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-176-20261123@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Expression of interest deadline: CARB-X 2026 Funding Round 2 – A
 ntibacterial Research (all themes)
DESCRIPTION:CARB-X. CARB-X's 2026 Funding Round Cycle 2 (all themes) accep
 ts expressions of interest from 10 November (10:00 ET) to 23 November 202
 6 (23:59 ET). The 2026 themes are direct-acting therapeutics for Gram-neg
 ative infections\, the Novel Chemistry for AMR Challenge (target-based th
 erapeutics)\, non-vaccine prevention of neonatal sepsis\, and neonatal se
 psis diagnostics. Invited applicants then submit a confidential project n
 arrative and budget (around early February 2027) and present to the Advis
 ory Board. Successful applicants must cost-share a percentage of the proj
 ect\, and the application page gives no per-award amounts.\n\nhttps://car
 b-x.org/apply/application-process/
URL:https://carb-x.org/apply/application-process/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-332-20261123@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: PharmaNL Shared Development Infrastructure 
 2026
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw / PharmaNL. ZonMw/PharmaNL round funding the set-up or u
 pgrade of shared infrastructure for developing\, scaling up and producing
  (innovative) medicines in the Netherlands\, in line with PharmaNL's May 
 2026 SDI investment agenda. Dutch companies and knowledge institutions ca
 n request up to EUR 5M (round budget EUR 23.3M) with 50% co-financing\; a
 t least half of the capacity must be opened to start-ups\, scale-ups and 
 academic groups at market prices. Project ideas are due 23 Nov 2026 (14:0
 0)\; invited full applications by 20 Apr 2027. Since a 10 Nov 2026 rectif
 ication\, projects may run until end of June 2031.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.n
 l/nl/subsidie/pharmanl-shared-development-infrastructure-2026
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/pharmanl-shared-development-infrastru
 cture-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-38-20261124@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Application deadline: MSCA Doctoral Networks 2026
DESCRIPTION:European Commission – MSCA. OPEN. The MSCA Doctoral Networks
  call HORIZON-MSCA-2026-DN-01 funds international doctoral training netwo
 rks that offer 3-year PhD positions with mobility. It opened on 28 May 20
 26 and closes on 24 November 2026 (17:00 Brussels time). REA lists an ind
 icative call budget of EUR 593.03M. A network of at least 3 organisations
  from 3 different countries is required\, and the division already runs t
 he EU2P programme.\n\nhttps://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu
 /actions/doctoral-networks
URL:https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/actions/doctoral-n
 etworks
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-200-20261127@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Utrechts Universiteitsfonds – Funding for 
 researchers (round 6\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Utrechts Universiteitsfonds. Grants for UU employees for resea
 rch visits abroad and for research and education costs (e.g. hiring help\
 , materials\, organising a congress)\, applied for through the UU subsidy
  portal. Six rounds per year\; not every fund type is open in every round
 \, and each fund has its own criteria.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/organisati
 on/donate/apply-for-subsidies/funding-for-researchers
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsidies/funding-f
 or-researchers
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-242-20261127@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Utrechts Universiteitsfonds – Student supp
 ort (international exchange/internship)\, round 6 2026
DESCRIPTION:Utrechts Universiteitsfonds. The Utrecht University Fund's stu
 dent programme helps fund an international exchange or internship\, for e
 xample a master's research internship abroad. Applicants must be a Studen
 t Friend of the Fund (€10 a year). Named funds within the Fund may set 
 their own criteria. About €80\,000 a year is available across all stude
 nt grants. In 2026 there are six rounds\, and round 6 runs from 2 to 27 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsi
 dies/grants-for-students
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/apply-for-subsidies/grants-fo
 r-students
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-264-20261127@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ROSANNA Fund for Women – 2026 application 
 round
DESCRIPTION:Utrechts Universiteitsfonds. Need-based grant from the Utrecht
 s Universiteitsfonds for talented women with a link to Utrecht University
 : up to EUR 4\,000 for researchers and EUR 3\,000 for students\, dependin
 g on the candidate's financial situation and needs. It can cover tuition\
 , living costs for a 3-9 month study or research stay\, or coaching and c
 ourses (not conferences). Round 6 is open 2-27 November 2026\, with appli
 cations through the UU Fund Portal.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/
 donate/rosanna-fund-for-women
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/organisation/donate/rosanna-fund-for-women
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-266-20261130@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Alzheimer Nederland Impuls Grant 2026 – Ro
 und 3
DESCRIPTION:Alzheimer Nederland. Alzheimer Nederland's Impuls Grant funds 
 dementia proposals that ZonMw/NWO rated highly in general (not dementia-s
 pecific) rounds such as Rubicon\, Open Competitie XS or Veni but rejected
  only for lack of budget\; the proposal must be submitted unchanged withi
 n 6 months of the rejection. Under the July 2025 call conditions\, applic
 ants need at least 4 years of dementia research experience and must be no
  more than 8 years past their PhD\, and up to €850\,000 is available pe
 r application. There are three assessment rounds a year\; the third 2026 
 round reportedly closes on 30 Nov 2026 at 12:00 via the AIMS portal (not 
 re-confirmed today).\n\nhttps://www.alzheimer-nederland.nl/onderzoek/voor
 -onderzoekers/alzheimer-nederland-impulssubsidie
URL:https://www.alzheimer-nederland.nl/onderzoek/voor-onderzoekers/alzheim
 er-nederland-impulssubsidie
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-284-20261130@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Application deadline: EAHP–EPSA Student Science Award 2027 (31st
  EAHP Congress\, Vienna)
DESCRIPTION:EAHP (European Association of Hospital Pharmacists). Award for
  the best hospital or clinical pharmacy research abstract by an EPSA memb
 er student\, who must be the main contributor and author. First ideas wer
 e due 12 October 2026\; the final abstract\, student involvement form and
  proof of student status are due 30 November 2026. Abstracts are judged o
 n relevance to hospital pharmacy\, scientific quality\, language and stru
 cture\, and student involvement. The winner is announced and presents at 
 the closing ceremony of the 31st EAHP Congress in Vienna in March 2027\; 
 no cash prize is listed.\n\nhttps://eahp.eu/about-us/students/eahp-epsa-s
 tudent-science-award/selection-procedure
URL:https://eahp.eu/about-us/students/eahp-epsa-student-science-award/sele
 ction-procedure
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-247-20261201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Rubicon 2026-3 (postdoc research abroad)
DESCRIPTION:NWO. Lets recent PhD graduates (PhD within 12 months before th
 e deadline\, or a supervisor's declaration that the thesis is approved) s
 pend 12–24 months at a research institute outside the Netherlands. It c
 overs salary\, travel and limited research costs\; the round budget of 
 €3\,145\,000 is shared across the four NWO domains. Applications are in
 dividual and due 1 December 2026\, 14:00.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/en/subs
 idy/rubicon-2026-3
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/rubicon-2026-3
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-281-20261201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Fulbright Grants for Dutch PhD Candidates 20
 27-2028 (research stay in the US)
DESCRIPTION:Fulbright Commission the Netherlands. USD 2\,000 per month (ma
 x USD 12\,000) plus partial health insurance for a 3–6 month research s
 tay at a US university/institute in 2027-2028. For PhD candidates with Du
 tch nationality affiliated with a Dutch university\; research in the US m
 ust be necessary. KNAW advises. Deadline 1 December 2026\, 12:00 noon Dut
 ch time. Note: patient-related clinical research may be excluded per cond
 itions\; check guide.\n\nhttps://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/promovendi/fulbr
 ight-beurzen-voor-promovendi/
URL:https://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/promovendi/fulbright-beurzen-voor-prom
 ovendi/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-282-20261201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Fulbright Grants for Dutch Scholars 2027-202
 8 (research/teaching in the US)
DESCRIPTION:Fulbright Commission the Netherlands. Two grants per year of U
 SD 15\,000 for scholars at Dutch universities/research institutions to do
  research and/or teach at a US university for 3–6 months in academic ye
 ar 2027-2028. KNAW advises. Deadline 1 December 2026\, 12:00 noon Dutch t
 ime.\n\nhttps://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/wetenschappers/fulbright-beurzen-
 2/
URL:https://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/wetenschappers/fulbright-beurzen-2/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-307-20261201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Klinische Fellows 2026
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. ZonMw's Clinical Fellows scheme lets medical specialist
 s with a PhD\, early in their research career\, set up their first own re
 search line alongside patient care. Up to €200\,000 per fellow for 36
 –60 months from a €2M round budget\; the institution must contribute 
 at least 25% (cash or in kind)\, and applications are in English with a c
 andidate profile and an embedding guarantee. Project ideas are due 1 Dece
 mber 2026 (14:00) via Mijn ZonMw\; invited full applications are due 11 M
 ay 2027 (14:00).\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/klinische-fellows-20
 26
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/klinische-fellows-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-280-20261204@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:Application deadline: HTAi 2027 Annual Meeting (Brussels) – Part
 icipation Grants
DESCRIPTION:HTAi (Health Technology Assessment international). Participati
 on grants help HTA stakeholders who could not otherwise attend the HTAi A
 nnual Meeting to present their work and join the global HTA community\; s
 ome grants are sponsored by external parties. For HTAi 2027 (12-16 June 2
 027\, Brussels) they are aimed at people from low- and middle-income coun
 tries\, patient and caregiver representatives\, and full-time students in
  HTA-related programmes. Applications are open and close on 4 December 20
 26. The grant amount and what it covers are not published on the grants p
 age.\n\nhttps://htai.org/about/awards-scholarships/htai-participation-gra
 nts/
URL:https://htai.org/about/awards-scholarships/htai-participation-grants/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-246-20261207@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: GGG – Alledaagse Aandoeningen in de huisa
 rtsenpraktijk (Common Conditions in General Practice)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Good Use of Medicines (GGG) round for research on quest
 ions from the NHG general-practice knowledge agenda\, aiming at more effe
 ctive\, safer or more efficient use of medicines already registered in th
 e Netherlands for common conditions. Total budget is €5 million with no
  fixed cap per project\; multicentre studies may be needed. Project ideas
  are due 7 December 2026\; invited full applications are due 31 May 2027\
 , with a decision expected end of October 2027. The applicant must take p
 art in UNH-Research through a university general-practice department.\n\n
 https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/alledaagse-aandoeningen-de-huisartsenpra
 ktijk
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/alledaagse-aandoeningen-de-huisartsen
 praktijk
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-333-20261207@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: Scientific Meetings and Consultations 2026 
 – 7 December 2026 cut-off
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO grant for organising a scientific meeting or consulta
 tion in the Netherlands. The NWO calls list (checked 14 Nov 2026) shows t
 he 2026 call as continuous with an upcoming submission date of 7 Dec 2026
 \, 14:00. Earlier rounds allowed up to EUR 15\,000 per meeting (consultat
 ions up to EUR 2\,400). The topic must fit an NWO Science domain\, so fra
 me pharmacoepi meetings around methods or data science. The instrument cl
 oses early if its budget runs out. Check the call page for the current co
 nditions.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/scientific-meetings-and-consulta
 tions-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/scientific-meetings-and-consultations-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-327-20261210@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Venture Challenge Spring 2027 (life sciences
  & health start-up programme)
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO's Venture Challenge is an 8-10 week programme for tea
 ms of three or four (including the scientist behind the discovery) planni
 ng a life sciences and health start-up\, for example around a therapy\, d
 iagnostic\, device or tool. It offers two three-day bootcamps (April and 
 June 2027)\, coaching and a final pitch to entrepreneurs and investors\; 
 teams pay a personal contribution of EUR 2\,000-2\,500 and the call budge
 t is EUR 100\,000. Applications are due 10 December 2026 (14:00 CET).\n\n
 https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/venture-challenge-spring-2027
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/venture-challenge-spring-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-323-20261211@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Passende Zorg – Doorbreken van systeembele
 mmeringen (2026)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Small ZonMw grant (max EUR 50\,000\, 12 months) under t
 he Kaderprogramma Passende Zorg for existing transmural or interdisciplin
 ary collaborations\, such as academic workplaces or learning and research
  networks\, to analyse system barriers and develop strategies for sustain
 ably applying proven appropriate Zvw care. Implementation itself and dire
 ct care costs are not funded. Applications (in Dutch) are handled first c
 ome\, first served until 11 December 2026 (14:00) or until the budget run
 s out\; decisions follow within three weeks.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/s
 ubsidie/doorbreken-van-systeembelemmeringen
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/doorbreken-van-systeembelemmeringen
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-308-20261215@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Nomination deadline: ISPOR Bernie J. O'Brien New Investigator Awar
 d 2027
DESCRIPTION:ISPOR. ISPOR award recognising an early-career researcher who 
 shows exceptional promise in health economics and outcomes research. Nomi
 nees must be ISPOR members within 7 years of their highest degree and wit
 hin 10 years of their first lead/corresponding-author outcomes research p
 aper\; the nominator needs at least 2 consecutive years of ISPOR membersh
 ip\, and self-nominations are allowed. The winner receives an unrestricte
 d USD 5\,000 grant plus free ISPOR Conference registration and travel/acc
 ommodation. Nominations are open 25 September to 15 December 2026.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/scientific-achievement-and-leaders
 hip-awards/bernie-obrien-new-investigator-award
URL:https://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/scientific-achievement-and-l
 eadership-awards/bernie-obrien-new-investigator-award
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-309-20261215@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Nomination deadline: ISPOR HEOR Excellence Award – Application 2
 027
DESCRIPTION:ISPOR. ISPOR award for an outstanding applied health outcomes 
 research publication with high (or expected high) impact on health policy
  or healthcare decision-making\, published in a peer-reviewed journal in 
 the preceding calendar year. Self-nominations are accepted\; a candidate 
 can be nominated for only one major ISPOR award per year. The recipient g
 ets free ISPOR Conference registration and travel/accommodation and is ho
 noured at the awards ceremony (no cash amount stated). Nominations are op
 en 25 September to 15 December 2026.\n\nhttps://www.ispor.org/about/award
 s-grants/scientific-achievement-and-leadership-awards/health-economics-an
 d-outcomes-research--application-award
URL:https://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/scientific-achievement-and-l
 eadership-awards/health-economics-and-outcomes-research--application-awar
 d
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-314-20261215@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Nomination deadline: ISPOR HEOR Excellence Award – Methodology 2
 027
DESCRIPTION:ISPOR. ISPOR award\, running since 1997\, for an outstanding p
 aper that advances health economics and outcomes research methodology and
  is expected to be widely adopted. The paper must have been published in 
 a peer-reviewed journal (print or Medline e-publication) in the preceding
  calendar year\; other outputs such as books and reports are also conside
 red. Self-nominations are accepted\, but a candidate can be nominated for
  only one major ISPOR award per year. The winner receives free ISPOR Conf
 erence registration plus travel and accommodation\, and is honoured at th
 e awards ceremony. No cash amount is stated. Applications are open 25 Sep
 tember to 15 December 2026.\n\nhttps://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/
 scientific-achievement-and-leadership-awards/health-economics-and-outcome
 s-research--methodology-award
URL:https://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/scientific-achievement-and-l
 eadership-awards/health-economics-and-outcomes-research--methodology-awar
 d
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-315-20261215@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Nomination deadline: ISPOR Impact Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:ISPOR. ISPOR award for health economics and outcomes research 
 with demonstrable real-world impact\, for example on regulatory\, reimbur
 sement or coverage decisions\, or on health policy. Entries must link the
  work to a clearly quantifiable outcome. Individuals or project teams any
 where in the world can be nominated\, and ISPOR membership is not require
 d for nominees. The nominator must be an ISPOR member and must submit a l
 etter of support\; self-nominations are allowed. The prize is an unrestri
 cted USD 10\,000 grant\, conference registration and travel for one repre
 sentative\, and a feature in an ISPOR publication. Applications are open 
 25 September to 15 December 2026.\n\nhttps://www.ispor.org/about/awards-g
 rants/scientific-achievement-and-leadership-awards/ispor-impact-award
URL:https://www.ispor.org/about/awards-grants/scientific-achievement-and-l
 eadership-awards/ispor-impact-award
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-197-20261222@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: Geneesmiddelen VIMP 2026-1 (Dissemination 
 & Implementation Impulse)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. VIMP (dissemination and implementation boost) within Zo
 nMw's Goed Gebruik Geneesmiddelen programme\, helping finished ZonMw-fund
 ed research on good medicine use (completed no more than three years ago)
  get used in practice\; dissemination alone is not enough. Max EUR 50\,00
 0 and 18 months per project from a EUR 250\,000 budget\; open since 22 Ju
 ne 2026\, deadline 22 December 2026\, 14:00\, though it may close earlier
  if the budget runs out. Applicant must be a legal entity in the Netherla
 nds\, and applications are in Dutch.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/
 geneesmiddelen-vimp-2026-1
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/geneesmiddelen-vimp-2026-1
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-299-20261224@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261225
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: USO Education Innovation 2027 (Utrechts Sti
 muleringsfonds Onderwijs)
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht University. Utrecht University's Stimuleringsfonds Ond
 erwijs (USO) funds cross-faculty education innovation projects of up to E
 UR 200\,000 for a maximum of three years\, normally starting in September
  2027. The three themes are feedback & assessment\, dialogue & debate\, a
 nd a free category aligned with the Strategic Plan 2030 and the Utrecht E
 ducational Model. Teachers had to register as consortium leader or member
  by 16 October 2026. The brief first-round proposal is due 24 December 20
 26 (12:00)\, and the developed second-round proposal is due 19 March 2027
 \, with pitches on 13 April 2027. Proposals must involve more than one fa
 culty and are submitted by the dean of the coordinating faculty.\n\nhttps
 ://www.uu.nl/en/news/call-for-proposals-uso-education-innovation-2027
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/news/call-for-proposals-uso-education-innovation-
 2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-154-20270101@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: KNMP Stipendiafonds (international study tr
 ip grant)
DESCRIPTION:KNMP. KNMP stipend for pharmacy students at Groningen\, Leiden
  and Utrecht who go abroad for at least two weeks for research that is pa
 rt of their pharmacy study\; applicant must be a candidate KNMP member an
 d must not have started the research yet. Applications are judged three t
 imes a year (closing dates 1 January\, 1 July and 1 October). A 'light' a
 pplication gives EUR 300-500\; a 'heavy' application (meeting at least tw
 o high-potential criteria) can give a higher\, unspecified amount. Each s
 tudent may apply only once.\n\nhttps://www.knmp.nl/beroepsontwikkeling/on
 derzoek/stipendiafonds
URL:https://www.knmp.nl/beroepsontwikkeling/onderzoek/stipendiafonds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-182-20270111@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270112
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Kolff+ Programme 2027 – Call 2
DESCRIPTION:Nierstichting (Dutch Kidney Foundation). The Dutch Kidney Foun
 dation's Kolff+ programme runs open-competition calls for Creativity\, Ju
 nior/Senior Talent and Success Accelerator grants\, with €1–1.5M per 
 call. The Kolff+ 2027 programme has two calls. Call 1 closed for pre-prop
 osals on 10 September 2026. Call 2 opens 26 November 2026\, takes pre-pro
 posals until 11 January 2027 and runs the invited full-proposal stage fro
 m 12 April to 1 July 2027. Applications go through MIDAS. Relevant for re
 search on drug-induced kidney injury and medication safety in kidney pati
 ents.\n\nhttps://nierstichting.nl/onderzoekers/grants-aanvragen/kolff-pro
 gramma-2027
URL:https://nierstichting.nl/onderzoekers/grants-aanvragen/kolff-programma
 -2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-77-20270112@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270113
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Consolidator Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. ERC Consolidator Grant 2027 for researchers 5-15 years af
 ter their PhD (extensions possible for e.g. parental leave). Up to EUR 2M
  for 5 years\, plus up to EUR 1M extra for justified costs. Bottom-up\, a
 ny research topic. The call opened 24 September 2026 and closes 12 Januar
 y 2027.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/consolidator-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/consolidator-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-231-20270114@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: ERA4Health IICS4all 2027 (JTC9) – Investi
 gator-Initiated Clinical Studies in Cardiovascular\, Autoimmune\, Metabol
 ic & Respiratory Diseases
DESCRIPTION:ERA4Health. ERA4Health's ninth joint transnational call (IICS4
 all 2027) funds pragmatic\, multinational phase III randomised investigat
 or-initiated studies (comparative-effectiveness and/or repurposing of off
 -patent drugs) in cardiovascular\, metabolic\, autoimmune and non-communi
 cable respiratory diseases\, with attention to inclusivity\, sex/gender a
 nd age\; cancer\, phase I/II\, observational and commercially driven stud
 ies are out of scope. Projects last up to 48 months and are expected to s
 tart in January-May 2028. The call was published on 27 October 2026: pre-
 proposals are due 14 January 2027\, 12:00 CET\, and invited full proposal
 s 14 June 2027\, 12:00 CEST. The participating funders (about 25\, incl. 
 Belgium/KCE\, Germany\, Norway\, Poland\, UK) do not include the Netherla
 nds/ZonMw\, and the total budget is not stated on the call page.\n\nhttps
 ://era4health.eu/calls/iics4all2027.php
URL:https://era4health.eu/calls/iics4all2027.php
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-162-20270115@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Application deadline: KHMW Proefschriftprijs Interdisciplinariteit
  2027
DESCRIPTION:KHMW. KHMW prize of €10\,000 for one strongly interdisciplin
 ary PhD thesis bridging the natural\, social and humanities sciences\, re
 searched at a Dutch institution. The 2027 edition is for PhDs awarded bet
 ween 1 September 2025 and 31 August 2026. Nominations come from at least 
 two professors at Dutch universities or other experts and are submitted w
 ith a CV\, a publication list and the thesis. Registration opens in Novem
 ber 2026 and the deadline is 15 January 2027.\n\nhttps://khmw.nl/khmw-pro
 efschriftprijs-interdisciplinariteit/
URL:https://khmw.nl/khmw-proefschriftprijs-interdisciplinariteit/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-275-20270115@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Nomination deadline: KNAW Faces of Science 2027 (PhD candidates\, 
 nomination)
DESCRIPTION:KNAW. KNAW network of about 12 new PhD candidates each year wh
 o share their research and life as a researcher through at least monthly 
 blogs or vlogs\, network meetings and science communication activities\; 
 financed by the Lira Foundation. Candidates must be in the first half of 
 their PhD at a university in the Kingdom of the Netherlands and are nomin
 ated by a KNAW member or a member or alumnus of De Jonge Akademie (one pe
 r year)\, or by NEMO Kennislink. Nominations opened on 15 October 2026 an
 d close on 15 January 2027.\n\nhttps://www.knaw.nl/en/science-funds/faces
 -science
URL:https://www.knaw.nl/en/science-funds/faces-science
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-124-20270118@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Longfonds Consortium Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:Longfonds. Longfonds funds research consortia working on the p
 revention\, treatment and cure of chronic lung diseases\, from fundamenta
 l and (pre)clinical research to public health and prevention. The 2027 ca
 ll opens on 23 November 2026 and offers two grants of up to EUR 700\,000 
 each\; the pre-application deadline is 18 January 2027\, 12:00 CET\, and 
 the full-proposal date is not yet published (2026 round: full proposals 1
 8 May). Patients must be involved from the start of proposal writing. Rel
 evant for consortia on respiratory drug safety\, inhaler adherence and CO
 PD/asthma pharmacotherapy.\n\nhttps://research.longfonds.nl/grants-and-ot
 her-support/consortium-grants
URL:https://research.longfonds.nl/grants-and-other-support/consortium-gran
 ts
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-211-20270119@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270120
SUMMARY:Application deadline: SSH Open Competition Explore 2027 – Round 
 1 (formerly XS)
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO's small SSH Open Competition grants (now called Explo
 re\, formerly XS) of up to EUR 50\,000 for innovative social sciences and
  humanities research lasting 6 to 24 months\, with a single applicant and
  no co-applicants\; total call budget EUR 4 million. Applicants need a Ph
 D and a paid position at an eligible research organisation\, and from 202
 7 they can apply right after their PhD. Only one Open Competition proposa
 l per calendar year is allowed\, and applicants must not have a running X
 S or Explore project. Round 1 closes on 19 January 2027 at 14:00 CET\, wi
 th further rounds expected in April and September 2027.\n\nhttps://www.nw
 o.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-explore-2027-round-1
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-explore-2027-round-1
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-311-20270119@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270120
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: ERA4Health NanoDiagNCD 2027 – Nano and Ad
 vanced Technologies for Diagnostic Tools in Non-Communicable Diseases
DESCRIPTION:ERA4Health. ERA4Health joint transnational call for translatio
 nal research using nanotechnology (alone or with other key enabling techn
 ologies) to build and validate diagnostic or theranostic tools for non-co
 mmunicable diseases. Projects must benchmark against existing diagnostics
  and address translation aspects such as scalability\, standardisation\, 
 regulatory readiness and cost-effectiveness\; biomarker discovery and inf
 ectious diseases are excluded. 36-month projects funded by participating 
 national/regional funders under their own rules\; opens 17 November 2026\
 , pre-proposals due 19 January 2027 (12:00)\, full-proposal date not yet 
 published.\n\nhttps://anr.fr/en/call-for-proposals-details/call/preannoun
 cement-era4health-2027-nano-and-advanced-technologies-for-developing-diag
 nostic-tools-to-i/
URL:https://anr.fr/en/call-for-proposals-details/call/preannouncement-era4
 health-2027-nano-and-advanced-technologies-for-developing-diagnostic-tool
 s-to-i/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-322-20270119@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270120
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Passende Zorg – Research initiated ronde 
 2: Onderzoek naar organisatie van passende zorg
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Round 2 of the Research Initiated line of ZonMw's Kader
 programma Passende Zorg funds research into interventions\, care pathways
  and organisational strategies that reduce inappropriate use of insured (
 Zvw\, or Zvw+Wlz) care and use capacity better\, looking at effects on he
 alth\, access\, workforce and costs. Up to EUR 1M per project for up to 4
  years (EUR 10M round budget). Two stages: intention-to-apply form by 8 D
 ecember 2026 and project idea by 19 January 2027 (14:00)\; invited full a
 pplications are due 28 September 2027. Applications in English with a Dut
 ch lay summary.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/research-initiated-ro
 nde-2-onderzoek-naar-organisatie-van-passende-zorg
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/research-initiated-ronde-2-onderzoek-
 naar-organisatie-van-passende-zorg
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-232-20270120@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270121
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: EP PerMed Joint Transnational Call 2027 –
  Cell and Gene Therapy for Personalised Medicine (CGT4PM2027)
DESCRIPTION:EP PerMed. EP PerMed published JTC2027 on cell and gene therap
 y for personalised medicine (CGT4PM2027) on 4 November 2026\, with about 
 EUR 38M from funders in 24 countries and 10 regions. ZonMw takes part for
  the Netherlands. The call funds multinational consortia that develop and
  validate novel somatic cell\, gene or combined therapies\, or related bi
 ological products\, in any disease area. Pre-proposals are due 20 January
  2027 and full proposals 25 May 2027 (both 14:00 CET/CEST)\; some nationa
 l deadlines differ.\n\nhttps://www.eppermed.eu/funding-projects/calls/jtc
 2027/
URL:https://www.eppermed.eu/funding-projects/calls/jtc2027/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-256-20270121@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270122
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: THCS Joint Transnational Call 2027 – Tran
 sforming the Health and Care Workforce for Sustainable and Resilient Syst
 ems
DESCRIPTION:THCS Partnership (Transforming Health and Care Systems). The H
 orizon Europe co-funded THCS partnership has pre-announced its 2027 joint
  transnational call\, 'Transforming the Health and Care Workforce for Sus
 tainable and Resilient Systems'\, which funds transnational consortia doi
 ng research on the health and care workforce. The call is scheduled for p
 ublication on 16 November 2026\, with pre-proposals due 21 January 2027 (
 14:00 CET) and full proposals due 24 June 2027 (14:00 CEST). The budget a
 nd participating funders are not yet published\; ZonMw hosts the joint ca
 ll secretariat. Relevant for workforce\, task-shifting and pharmacy-pract
 ice and health-services research.\n\nhttps://www.thcspartnership.eu/fundi
 ng/jtc-2027-pre-announcement.kl
URL:https://www.thcspartnership.eu/funding/jtc-2027-pre-announcement.kl
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-283-20270121@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270122
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Fulbright Grants for Dutch Graduate Students
  2027-2028 (study in the US)
DESCRIPTION:Fulbright Commission the Netherlands. About 6 grants of up to 
 USD 50\,000 for Dutch nationals (with a bachelor's degree) to follow a gr
 aduate programme\, non-degree programme or research period of at least 9 
 months at a US university in 2027-2028\; partial health insurance include
 d. Not for the first year of a full US PhD. Deadline 21 January 2027.\n\n
 https://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/ik-ben-student/fulbright-beurzen/
URL:https://fulbright.nl/naar-de-vs/ik-ben-student/fulbright-beurzen/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-136-20270125@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270126
SUMMARY:Application deadline: NNF Start Package Grants for Faculty Recruit
 ment Q1 2027
DESCRIPTION:Novo Nordisk Foundation. Novo Nordisk Foundation start package
 s help Danish universities\, hospitals and non-profit research institutio
 ns recruit researchers of any nationality into faculty positions and set 
 up independent groups. The host institution applies\; grants run for 4 ye
 ars\, up to DKK 5M (assistant professor/tenure track)\, DKK 8M (associate
  professor) or DKK 10M (full or clinical professor). The Q1 2027 round op
 ened on 8 October 2026 and closes on 25 January 2027 at 14:00 Copenhagen 
 time. Only relevant for researchers moving to a Danish institution.\n\nht
 tps://novonordiskfonden.dk/en/grant/start-package-grants-for-faculty-recr
 uitment-q1-2027/
URL:https://novonordiskfonden.dk/en/grant/start-package-grants-for-faculty
 -recruitment-q1-2027/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-183-20270126@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270127
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: Veni – ZonMw Health Research Domain 2026
 /2027
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO Veni in the ZonMw Health Research and Development dom
 ain: up to EUR 320\,000 for up to three years for researchers with a PhD 
 obtained within three years before 1 January 2026 (or between 1 January a
 nd 2 September 2026). The pre-proposal deadline was 1 September 2026 and 
 no new applications are possible. Applicants with a positive pre-proposal
  decision submit full proposals by 26 January 2027\, 14:00 CET.\n\nhttps:
 //www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-veni-health-research-and-devel
 opment-zonmw-2026
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talent-programme-veni-health-research-
 and-development-zonmw-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-258-20270128@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270129
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: ERDERA Networking Support Scheme (rare dise
 ase networking events)
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe – ERDERA. Funds transnational networking even
 ts on rare diseases or rare cancers\, in person or hybrid\, that bring to
 gether researchers\, clinicians\, research managers and patient organisat
 ions. It pays up to EUR 30\,000 per event\, including VAT and participant
 s' travel and accommodation. Groups of 3-10 co-applicants from at least t
 hree countries apply\, including at least one from an underrepresented co
 untry (e.g. Ireland\, Poland\, Portugal\, Greece). The call is permanentl
 y open with periodic collection dates until funds run out (expected April
  2029). The next cut-off is 28 Jan 2027\, 12:00 CET (round NSS2027A)\, an
 d its funding depends on the EC confirming ERDERA's second funding phase\
 , expected Q1 2027.\n\nhttps://erdera.org/call/networking-support-scheme-
 nss/
URL:https://erdera.org/call/networking-support-scheme-nss/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-190-20270201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: KNAW Early Career Partnerships 2026
DESCRIPTION:KNAW. KNAW Early Career Partnerships: up to EUR 10\,000 to org
 anise an interdisciplinary science meeting\, for researchers who obtained
  their PhD three to seven years before 2027 and work at a university or r
 esearch institute in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (KNAW extension rules
  apply). Up to ten partnerships are awarded each year. The 2027 round is 
 open until 1 February 2027.\n\nhttps://www.knaw.nl/en/science-funds/knaw-
 early-career-partnerships
URL:https://www.knaw.nl/en/science-funds/knaw-early-career-partnerships
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-195-20270201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: EUP OHAMR Joint Transnational Call 2027 –
  Understand\, Model and Stop AMR Transmission
DESCRIPTION:EUP OHAMR. EUP OHAMR's 2027 joint transnational call funds res
 earch on understanding\, modelling and stopping AMR transmission. It cove
 rs transmission-dynamics modelling\, the role of host commensal microbes 
 (including fungi) and selective decolonisation\, and tools to reduce resi
 stant microbes and genes in environmental hotspots. About EUR 28M in tota
 l comes from 33 funders in 26 countries\, with ZonMw funding Dutch partne
 rs. Consortia need 3-6 partners (7 in some cases) from at least 3 countri
 es\; the call opens 18 Nov 2026\, with pre-proposals due 1 Feb 2027 and f
 ull proposals 23 Jun 2027.\n\nhttps://ohamr.eu/2026/10/19/pre-announcment
 -call-to-advance-research-on-amr-transmission/
URL:https://ohamr.eu/2026/10/19/pre-announcment-call-to-advance-research-o
 n-amr-transmission/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-328-20270201@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:Application deadline: EFSD and Novo Nordisk A/S Programme for Diab
 etes Research in Europe 2027
DESCRIPTION:EFSD (European Foundation for the Study of Diabetes). Project 
 grants for basic or clinical diabetes research (clinical meaning studies 
 in humans on clinically relevant diabetes topics) carried out at non-prof
 it institutions in Europe or associated countries. Grants are generally u
 p to EUR 100\,000\, with EUR 100\,000-250\,000 considered in exceptional 
 cases\; duration one year or longer. EASD membership is encouraged but no
 t required\, and investigators may hold only one EASD/EFSD grant at a tim
 e. Applications through the EFSD Programme Portal by 1 February 2027 (12:
 00 CET)\; decisions expected May 2027.\n\nhttps://www.europeandiabetesfou
 ndation.org/programmes/programme-calls/efsd-and-novo-nordisk-as-programme
 -for-diabetes-research-in-europe-call/
URL:https://www.europeandiabetesfoundation.org/programmes/programme-calls/
 efsd-and-novo-nordisk-as-programme-for-diabetes-research-in-europe-call/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-329-20270215@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270216
SUMMARY:Application deadline: EFSD and Lilly Young Investigator Research A
 ward Programme 2027
DESCRIPTION:EFSD (European Foundation for the Study of Diabetes). Research
  awards of EUR 50\,000 for early-career scientists and clinicians in diab
 etes and its complications\, up to 7 years after their most recent degree
  (PhD\, MSc or MD\; extensions for e.g. parental leave or illness). Appli
 cants must have a track record in diabetes research\, may not hold a perm
 anent appointment\, and must hold the award at a non-profit institution i
 n Europe or an associated country. The EFSD overview page lists the 2027 
 deadline as 15 February 2027\; the scheme page still shows the 2026 round
 \, so check details when it is updated.\n\nhttps://www.europeandiabetesfo
 undation.org/programmes/programme-calls/efsd-and-lilly-young-investigator
 -research-award-programme/
URL:https://www.europeandiabetesfoundation.org/programmes/programme-calls/
 efsd-and-lilly-young-investigator-research-award-programme/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-22-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Application deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027 Adverse Drug Reactions –
  Personalised Approaches
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-CARE-02 (RIA\, single sta
 ge): personalised approaches to reduce adverse drug reactions in patients
  taking three or more medicines\, especially with comorbidities. Proposal
 s should combine pharmacogenomics and other biomarkers for stratification
  with EHRs\, AI and clinical decision support\, assess clinical utility a
 nd cost-effectiveness\, and feed results into EMA and national (de)prescr
 ibing guidance. EUR 38M for about 4 projects of EUR 8-10M\; highly releva
 nt for PECP. The call opened on 29 October 2026 and closes on 17 February
  2027 at 17:00 Brussels time\, as confirmed by HaDEA's announcement of th
 e published 2027 Health calls.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tende
 rs/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2
 027-01-care-02
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-care-02
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-46-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-TOOL-01-two-stage – 
 AI for Predictive Biomarkers in Chronic NCDs
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Horizon Europe two-stage RIA HORIZON-HLTH-2027
 -02-TOOL-01-two-stage: developing predictive biomarkers of disease progre
 ssion and treatment response with AI methods for chronic non-communicable
  diseases. EUR 44.2M for about 6 projects of EUR 6-8M. Highly relevant fo
 r the division's AI/data science and pharmacoepi work. The call opened on
  29 October 2026\; the first-stage deadline is 17 February 2027 (17:00 Br
 ussels) and the second-stage deadline 16 September 2027\, as confirmed by
  HaDEA.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal
 /screen/opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-02-tool-01-two-stag
 e
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-02-tool-01-two-stage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-132-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Application deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEASE-08 – New Anti
 bacterial & Antifungal Therapies
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Horizon Europe RIA HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEAS
 E-08 for innovative antimicrobials against resistant pathogens\; each pro
 posal targets one of CRAB\, CRE/third-generation cephalosporin-resistant 
 Enterobacterales\, carbapenem-resistant P. aeruginosa\, MRSA\, drug-resis
 tant Aspergillus fumigatus or drug-resistant Candida (phage therapies out
  of scope). EUR 44.2M for about 5 projects of EUR 8-10M. The call opened 
 on 29 October 2026 and closes on 17 February 2027 at 17:00 Brussels time\
 , as confirmed by HaDEA's announcement of the published 2027 Health calls
 .\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/scree
 n/opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-disease-08
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-disease-08
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-142-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Application deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-ENVHLTH-02 – Climate-
 related Exposures in the Human Exposome
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Horizon Europe RIA (call HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01\
 , single stage) on integrating climate-related exposures such as heat\, a
 ir pollution and drought into large human exposome studies and modelling 
 how the exposome shifts under climate change. Projects should use AI and 
 real-world data\, address social and demographic vulnerability\, include 
 social sciences and humanities\, and share outputs via IHEN platforms and
  the European Climate and Health Observatory. EUR 45M for about 4 project
 s of EUR 10-11M. The call opened on 29 October 2026 and closes on 17 Febr
 uary 2027 at 17:00 Brussels time\, as confirmed by HaDEA's announcement o
 f the published 2027 Health calls.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-t
 enders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hl
 th-2027-01-envhlth-02
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-envhlth-02
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-143-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Application deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEASE-05/06/07 – An
 tivirals & Monoclonal Antibodies
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Three single-stage RIA topics in call HORIZON-
 HLTH-2027-01: DISEASE-05 novel small-molecule antivirals for pathogens wi
 th epidemic potential (EUR 44.2M\, ~5 projects of EUR 9-11M)\, DISEASE-06
  monoclonal antibodies against flaviviruses and DISEASE-07 monoclonal ant
 ibodies against filo-\, nairo-\, phenui-\, picorna- and togaviruses (each
  EUR 37.3M\, ~4 projects of EUR 9-10M). Work runs from discovery to GMP b
 atches and first-in-human safety studies\; relevant mainly as a partner f
 or clinical pharmacology and safety work packages. The call opened on 29 
 October 2026 and closes on 17 February 2027 at 17:00 Brussels time\, as c
 onfirmed by HaDEA's announcement of the published 2027 Health calls.\n\nh
 ttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/oppo
 rtunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-disease-05
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/horizon-hlth-2027-01-disease-05
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-250-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-01 – Innovat
 ive Healthcare Interventions for Non-Communicable Diseases (two-stage)
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Research and Innovation Action (HORIZON-HLTH-2
 027-02-DISEASE-01-two-stage) funding early-stage (phase 1/2 for drugs) cl
 inical trials of new or refined pharmacological or non-pharmacological in
 terventions for cardiovascular disease\, diabetes\, chronic respiratory d
 isease or chronic kidney disease. Applicants need prior proof-of-concept 
 and a draft protocol\, plus a health-economic assessment and real-world d
 ata analysis\; comparative-effectiveness studies are out of scope. EUR 63
 .8M in total\, about EUR 7-8M per project. The call opened on 29 October 
 2026\; the first-stage deadline is 17 February 2027 (17:00 Brussels) and 
 the second-stage deadline 16 September 2027\, as confirmed by HaDEA.\n\nh
 ttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/oppo
 rtunities/topic-details/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-01-two-stage
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-01-two-stage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-251-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEASE-10 – Chroni
 c NCDs in Children and Young People (GACD implementation research)
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Implementation research (HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-
 DISEASE-10\, GACD) on preventing\, screening\, diagnosing and managing ch
 ronic non-communicable diseases in people aged 1-24 in low- and middle-in
 come countries and/or underserved high-income populations. Projects must 
 use hybrid effectiveness-implementation designs and equitable HIC-LMIC le
 adership\; pharmacological trials and aetiological cohorts are excluded. 
 Expected EU contribution is EUR 3-4M per project (about 3 projects). The 
 call opened on 29 October 2026 and closes on 17 February 2027 at 17:00 Br
 ussels time\, as confirmed by HaDEA's announcement of the published 2027 
 Health calls.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/
 portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEASE-10
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-01-DISEASE-10
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-252-20270217@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-14 – Clinica
 l Trials for Neurodegenerative Diseases (two-stage)
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Research and Innovation Action (HORIZON-HLTH-2
 027-02-DISEASE-14-two-stage) for clinical trials that advance innovative 
 interventions for neurodegenerative diseases. Expected EU contribution is
  around EUR 10M per project (about 4 projects)\; check the topic page for
  the detailed scope. The call opened on 29 October 2026\; the first-stage
  deadline is 17 February 2027 (17:00 Brussels) and the second-stage deadl
 ine 16 September 2027\, as confirmed by HaDEA.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/in
 fo/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-detail
 s/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-14-two-stage
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/
 opportunities/topic-details/HORIZON-HLTH-2027-02-DISEASE-14-two-stage
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-244-20270301@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Application deadline: VSBfonds Beurs 2027 (study/research abroad a
 fter bachelor)
DESCRIPTION:VSBfonds. VSBfonds scholarship for recent bachelor's or master
 's graduates of Dutch universities and universities of applied sciences t
 o study abroad full-time for 3 to 24 months\, with departure between 1 Ju
 ly 2027 and 30 June 2028. It cannot be part of a Dutch degree programme\,
  and internships and online study do not qualify. Dutch nationality is th
 e standard requirement\, financial need must be shown\, and the grant is 
 up to EUR 7\,000 (up to EUR 10\,000 for a two-year programme). The single
  2027 round opens in November 2026 and closes on 1 March 2027.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.vsbfonds.nl/studiebeurzen/hbowo/beurs-aanvragen
URL:https://www.vsbfonds.nl/studiebeurzen/hbowo/beurs-aanvragen
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-320-20270301@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: Dynamics of Youth Invigoration Grants & Ope
 n Call – review point 1 March 2027
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht University – Dynamics of Youth. The UU strategic the
 me Dynamics of Youth funds two kinds of request. Invigoration Grants supp
 ort new research that reuses existing\, certified data\, tools or methods
 \, such as youth cohorts or registries. The Open Call covers activities t
 hat strengthen DoY and its communities\, such as events\, visiting fellow
 ships\, conference travel and FAIRification. Proposals must fit the DoY m
 ission on children and youth and support open science. Open Call requests
  up to EUR 2\,500 are reviewed all year. Larger requests and Invigoration
  Grants are reviewed at fixed points: 1 March\, 7 June and 4 October 2027
 . No amounts are stated.\n\nhttps://www.uu.nl/en/research/dynamics-of-you
 th/research/funding
URL:https://www.uu.nl/en/research/dynamics-of-youth/research/funding
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-206-20270309@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Vici – Science Domain 2027
DESCRIPTION:NWO. NWO Talent Programme grant of up to EUR 1.5M for senior r
 esearchers (PhD within 15 years of the benchmark date) to build a researc
 h group. NWO has posted the Vici Science (ENW) 2027 call as 'in preparati
 on': pre-proposals are due 9 March 2027\, 14:00\, and full proposals 7 Se
 ptember 2027\, 14:00. The call text is not yet approved\, so details may 
 still change.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talentprogramma-vici-enw
 -2027
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/nwo-talentprogramma-vici-enw-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-225-20270310@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270311
SUMMARY:Next cut-off deadline: ERC Proof of Concept 2027 (cut-offs Mar & S
 ep 2027)
DESCRIPTION:ERC. Lump sum of €150\,000 over 18 months for current or rec
 ent ERC grantees who want to test the commercial or societal potential of
  results from their ERC project. Under ERC Work Programme 2027 the call E
 RC-2027-PoC opens 12 November 2026 and has two cut-offs\, 10 March 2027 a
 nd 16 September 2027 (budget €60M\, ~400 grants). The ERC calls these d
 ates provisional.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/proof-concept
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/proof-concept
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-343-20270324@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270324
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270325
SUMMARY:Application deadline: PhD Studentship Scheme 2027
DESCRIPTION:Pharmacy Research UK. Pharmacy Research UK funds a full- or pa
 rt-time PhD of up to GBP 100\,000 (stipend\, research costs and fees) for
  UK-registered pharmacists and pharmacy technicians\; pre-registration tr
 ainees may apply if registered before the award starts. Projects must be 
 about pharmacy practice\; lab-based research is not funded\, and part-fun
 ding from another institution is welcome. The 2027 round opens 16 Novembe
 r 2026 and closes 24 March 2027 (13:00 UK time)\; interviews 7 July 2027\
 , final outcome 30 July 2027. Relevant to the division mainly as a UK par
 tner or co-supervisor.\n\nhttps://pharmacyresearchuk.org/for-researchers/
 personal-awards-2/personal-research-awards/
URL:https://pharmacyresearchuk.org/for-researchers/personal-awards-2/perso
 nal-research-awards/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-248-20270330@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Application deadline: NAM Collaboration Grant 2026 (animal-free me
 thods knowledge transfer)
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. Small grants of up to €30\,000 for up to 12 months to
  transfer animal-free methods (New Approach Methodologies such as organ-o
 n-chip systems and organoids) between a transferring lab and a receiving 
 lab at Dutch research organisations. Each partner must account for at lea
 st 20% of the budget. Applications are assessed in order of arrival until
  30 March 2027\, and the call may close early if the money runs out.\n\nh
 ttps://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/nam-collaboration-grant-2026
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/en/subsidy/nam-collaboration-grant-2026
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-324-20270330@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: Gravitation 2027 – Frontier Research for
  Consortia (Zwaartekracht)
DESCRIPTION:NWO. Seventh Gravitation round funding ten-year consortia of u
 p to six leading PIs (coordinator plus up to five co-PIs) from one or mor
 e disciplines\, with EUR 10M to 22.75M per consortium and about EUR 159M 
 in total. Only university Executive Boards may submit\, with at most four
  proposals per university\, so internal university selection comes first.
  Full proposals are due 30 March 2027 (14:00 CET)\; assessment includes r
 eferee review\, rebuttal and interviews.\n\nhttps://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/g
 ravitation-2027-frontier-research-for-consortia
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/gravitation-2027-frontier-research-for-con
 sortia
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-296-20270331@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Application deadline: BPS Dunlop Prize 2027 (clinical pharmacology
  research visit to Australasia)
DESCRIPTION:British Pharmacological Society (BPS). A prize\, given every t
 wo years\, for early-career clinical BPS members (clinical trainees\, con
 sultants up to 3 years after appointment\, lecturers\, senior lecturers).
  It pays for a 3-week research visit to Australasia\, co-supported by ASC
 EPT\, plus a lecture. The page body says up to GBP 5\,000 for travel and 
 subsistence\, but its meta text says GBP 500 plus expenses. Applicants ne
 ed 2 years of BPS membership\, must be based outside Australasia\, and mu
 st arrange a host in advance.\n\nhttps://www.bps.ac.uk/membership-communi
 ty/prizes-awards-grants-bursaries/prizes-awards-grants/article/dunlop-pri
 ze/
URL:https://www.bps.ac.uk/membership-community/prizes-awards-grants-bursar
 ies/prizes-awards-grants/article/dunlop-prize/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-113-20270405@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270405
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270406
SUMMARY:Pre-proposal deadline: Longfonds Junior Investigator Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:Longfonds. Longfonds Junior Investigator Grants support resear
 chers within five years of their PhD with up to EUR 250\,000 over three y
 ears (2026 amounts\; 2027 amounts not yet re-confirmed). Two-stage proced
 ure with a pre-application and then a full proposal\; patient involvement
  is required. The Longfonds grants overview lists the 2027 round as openi
 ng 8 January 2027 with a pre-application deadline of 5 April 2027\; the f
 ull-proposal date is not yet published.\n\nhttps://research.longfonds.nl/
 subsidies/jong-talent
URL:https://research.longfonds.nl/subsidies/jong-talent
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-101-20270511@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270511
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270512
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Synergy Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. ERC Synergy Grants fund 2-4 PIs\, one of them the corresp
 onding PI\, who work together on an ambitious problem in any research fie
 ld. The grant is up to EUR 10 million over six years\, plus up to EUR 4 m
 illion more for start-up costs\, major equipment or large facilities. The
  2027 call opens 17 February 2027 and closes 11 May 2027. The 2027 Work P
 rogramme also limits how many proposals a researcher may submit. A good f
 it for cross-disciplinary pharmacoepi\, HTA and data science collaboratio
 ns.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/synergy-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/synergy-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-292-20270513@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270513
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270514
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Zorgevaluatie en Gepast Gebruik (ZE&GG) – 
 Impactvolle kennisvragen uit de MSZ – Ronde 3
DESCRIPTION:ZonMw. ZonMw round in the Zorgevaluatie en Gepast Gebruik prog
 ramme that funds evaluation research addressing high-impact knowledge que
 stions from Dutch medical specialist care (MSZ). The ZonMw open-calls ove
 rview lists it as open with a deadline of 13 May 2027. The call page itse
 lf could not be read\, so eligibility\, budget and stages are not verifie
 d\; check the call page before applying.\n\nhttps://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsi
 die/zorgevaluatie-en-gepast-gebruik-impactvolle-kennisvragen-uit-de-msz-r
 onde-3
URL:https://www.zonmw.nl/nl/subsidie/zorgevaluatie-en-gepast-gebruik-impac
 tvolle-kennisvragen-uit-de-msz-ronde-3
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-216-20270701@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Longfonds-Swierenga Grant 2027 – Rare Lung
  Disease Research
DESCRIPTION:Longfonds. Up to EUR 50\,000 for a one-year project by an earl
 y-career researcher (PhD or confirmed defence date\; also clinicians\, re
 sidents or nurses with a research track record) at a Dutch university\, U
 MC\, KNAW/NKI institute or hospital\, on rare pulmonary diseases only (as
 thma\, COPD and lung cancer excluded). The grant is offered annually 2025
 -2029 and each applicant can receive it only once. According to the Longf
 onds grants overview the 2027 call opens 8 April 2027 with an application
  deadline of 1 July 2027\, 12:00 CET.\n\nhttps://research.longfonds.nl/gr
 ants-and-other-support/longfonds-swierenga-grant
URL:https://research.longfonds.nl/grants-and-other-support/longfonds-swier
 enga-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-337-20270730@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270731
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Longfonds-ERS Fellowship Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:Longfonds. A new fellowship from Longfonds and the European Re
 spiratory Society\, announced on the Longfonds grants overview as an inte
 rnational 2027 call with one grant. The call opens 30 May 2027 and applic
 ations are due 30 Jul 2027 (12:00 CET). The amount\, eligibility and scop
 e are not yet published\; Longfonds says more information follows in Janu
 ary 2027. Lung-disease research\, including pharmacotherapy or drug-utili
 sation questions in asthma or COPD\, could fit\, depending on the final c
 onditions.\n\nhttps://research.longfonds.nl/grants-and-other-support
URL:https://research.longfonds.nl/grants-and-other-support
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-196-20270826@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270827
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Advanced Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. ERC Advanced Grant 2027 (Work Programme 2027) for establi
 shed research leaders with a strong track record\, in any field\, hosted 
 in an EU Member State or associated country. Up to €2.5M over 5 years\,
  plus up to €1M for start-up costs/major equipment and up to €2M extr
 a for PIs moving from a non-associated third country. Call opens 27 May 2
 027\; deadline 26 August 2027. Successor to the 2026 round (ID 25).\n\nht
 tps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/advanced-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/advanced-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-226-20270901@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:Application deadline: ERC Plus Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ERC. Second round of the ERC Plus Grant: up to €7M per proje
 ct for transformative\, high-ambition research\, open to PIs at any caree
 r stage. ERC Work Programme 2027 gives ERC-2027-PLUS a provisional openin
 g of 1 June 2027 and a deadline of 1 September 2027\, with a budget of 
 €210M and about 30 grants.\n\nhttps://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/erc-plu
 s-grant
URL:https://erc.europa.eu/apply-grant/erc-plus-grant
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-253-20270916@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270917
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-03-TOOL-04 – Virtual H
 uman Twins for Clinical Decision Support in Prevention and Diagnosis
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Research and Innovation Action to build and cl
 inically validate multi-scale\, patient-specific Virtual Human Twin model
 s that support prevention and diagnosis\, including health-economic or co
 st-effectiveness evidence from real-world settings and plans for regulato
 ry compliance (MDR/IVDR\, AI Act). Expected EU contribution is €10–12
  million per project (about 4 projects). The single-stage call opens 3 Ju
 ne 2027 and closes 16 September 2027.\n\nhttps://cordis.europa.eu/program
 me/id/HORIZON_HORIZON-HLTH-2027-03-TOOL-04
URL:https://cordis.europa.eu/programme/id/HORIZON_HORIZON-HLTH-2027-03-TOO
 L-04
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-254-20270916@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270917
SUMMARY:Full proposal deadline: HORIZON-HLTH-2027-03-TOOL-08 – Next Gene
 ration of Frontier AI Models for Healthcare (CSA)
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe. Coordination and Support Action (a single proj
 ect of around €2.9 million) on preparing the next generation of frontie
 r AI models for healthcare. The single-stage call opens 3 June 2027 and c
 loses 16 September 2027. The detailed scope was not read\, so check the w
 ork programme.\n\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities
 /docs/2021-2027/horizon/wp-call/2026-2027/wp-4-health_horizon-2026-2027_e
 n.pdf
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/docs/2021-2027
 /horizon/wp-call/2026-2027/wp-4-health_horizon-2026-2027_en.pdf
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:funding-watch-339-20270916@robheerdink-collab.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261114T043746Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270917
SUMMARY:Application deadline: Mission Cancer 2027 – CANCER-03 Phase 1 an
 d First-in-Human Trials of Biomarker-Guided or Multi-Modal Treatments for
  Rare Cancers
DESCRIPTION:Horizon Europe – Mission Cancer. Research and innovation act
 ion (lump sum) in the Mission Cancer 2027 call (HORIZON-MISS-2027-02) for
  multi-centre phase 1/first-in-human trials of biomarker-guided medicines
  or multi-modal treatments for patients with rare or very rare cancers\, 
 including completing preclinical validation and considering drug repurpos
 ing\; innovative designs such as basket\, umbrella or adaptive trials are
  welcome. Proposals must show proof of regulatory advice on the trial des
 ign\, involve regional/national health authorities and join the Mission's
  'Diagnosis and treatment' cluster. EUR 7–9M per project (EUR 24M\, ~3 
 projects). Opens 10 Feb 2027\, deadline 16 Sep 2027 (official Missions wo
